James asked how to convert an amount of money (e.g., 10 reais) into PPP-equivalent terms. I explained the calculation process using PPP conversion factors and the importance of choosing the relevant year and type (GDP or household consumption) for the conversion. He then inquired about the differences between converting reais to USD versus using national deflators. I detailed the two approaches: converting to current USD then deflating versus deflating in reais first, highlighting that they yield different results due to nominal exchange rate variations and inflation differentials. I also discussed the implications of using an incorrect hybrid method and concluded with guidelines for appropriate treatments based on the objectives, emphasizing the distinct purposes of real USD, real BRL, and PPP international dollars for comparisons across countries.
